RETIRED 2026-09-07 by agent session, per user instruction.

This patch added a full port of the Rockchip vendor `gt9xx` touchscreen driver
(from armbian/linux-rockchip, branch rk-6.1-rkr7.2) to mainline kernel 6.18,
together with the RK3308BS GT911 "fold-fix" coordinate correction baked into
`gtp_touch_down`. It shipped in image v112/v113/v114.

Why it was tried
----------------
The GT911 on this board (Artillery M1 Pro S1-SOC) reports its horizontal axis
in a folded "double-width" space (a hard dead gap at chip-native X [350..749]).
We suspected the vendor driver / factory config might handle the panel
differently than mainline `goodix.c`, so we ported it and reprogrammed the chip
with the factory 1080x1920 config blob.

What we learned
---------------
1. The fold is INTRINSIC to the digitizer -- it appeared identically under
   mainline goodix.c (v111), the vendor gt9xx driver + factory blob (v112), and
   the vendor gt9xx driver + the chip's own config (v113). Neither the driver
   nor the config is the variable.
2. The v114 fold-fix (baked into the vendor driver) DID linearise the axis --
   the inch-mark test confirmed a clean, monotonic sweep through the old dead
   zone. BUT the vendor driver's multi-touch handling let the GT911's phantom
   secondary contacts through: ~46% of frames near the old fold reported 2-3
   contacts spread up to ~110 units apart, i.e. the long-standing "double touch"
   the user reported. In a single-touch KlipperScreen UI that risks phantom
   taps and accidental gestures.
3. The user confirmed from direct experience that mainline `goodix.c` did NOT
   exhibit the phantom double-touch (its input_mt_sync_frame +
   INPUT_MT_DROP_UNUSED handling is cleaner).

Superseded by
-------------
The fold-fix was ported to the mainline goodix.c report path instead, as a
small single-concern patch:

    patches/0015-input-touchscreen-goodix-rk3308bs-fold-fix.patch

That keeps mainline's clean multi-touch de-duplication AND applies our
coordinate correction. The DT node was reverted from `goodix,gt9xx` back to
`goodix,gt911` (patch 0001 + build-fork config/boards DTS), and
CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_GT9XX=y was removed from the build-fork kernel config
(CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_GOODIX=m is retained).

Retained (not deleted) in case the vendor driver is ever needed again for a
hardware variant mainline cannot support. The pristine vendor source remains in
the workspace at linux-rockchip-vendor/ and the validated userspace remapper at
tools/gt9xx-unfold-remapper.c.
